        return Err(io::Error::last_os_error());
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

By using `io::Error::last_os_error()`, you ensure that system call failures are recognized as standard I/O errors, allowing you to use standard Rust error handling mechanisms (like `io::Result` or `io::ErrorKind`) to inspect or report them.

